6-31337 (high severity: unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays).\n\n- Affected: <2.9.4, >=3.0.0 <3.1.0; fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0.\n- Chose 2.9.4, the minimal fixed version on the current 2.x line, to avoid a major-version upgrade.\n- Updated CHANGELOG.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 3a05f1e86f.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fastjson-cve-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but its reviewer list came back empty, so I'll request alex directly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VXYZH2SPsoZquQRzjoWKo6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, which fixes CVE-2026-31337. CI passed and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Version choice:** The advisory says the bug (high severity, unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays) is fixed in 2.9.4 and 3.1.0. I went with 2.9.4 because it stays on the 2.x line, so there's no major-version upgrade.\n- **Branch:** `fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337` has one commit (3a05f1e86f) that updates `requirements.txt` and adds a security note to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). It came back with no reviewers attached, so I added alex in a separate review request, and that one went through.\n\nI haven't merged it. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}